  "body": "## What changed\n\n`testdata/models/sample_ap214.step` laid flat could not be machined by 3D Finish or 3D Pocket. Both were refused with \"invalid machining parameters: chords meet 3+ ways at z = ...: non-manifold contact\".\n\n**Cause.** The model is three closed solids. Two of them are stacked so that, laid flat, their cylindrical walls overlap in Z (1.5875 .. 3.175) on the same vertical seam lines. Every plane in that band meets both outlines at the same 93 points, with four chords at each. Those chords run the same way and are subdivided differently, so welding coincident chords would not apply. `slice()` needs exactly two chords per end, so it refused, and `from_slice` reported the refusal as a parameter error.\n\n**Fix** (`crates/geometry/src/geometry/slice_bodies.rs`, new):\n- `slice()` keeps its plain read. Only when that read returns `NonManifold` does it retry as the union of the soup's closed solids:\n  - the facets are split into bodies by shared-edge connectivity (corners welded within 0.1 um, spatial hash);\n  - the retry runs only when every body is a closed, consistently wound 2-manifold with positive signed volume;\n  - each body is then sliced on its own and the sections are united with the 2D boolean union. This is the same law `material_above_of` already applies to bodies from separate entities (M13.11).\n- Everything else keeps the refusal:\n  - solids welded along a shared edge or face (they share it four ways, so they read as one non-manifold shell);\n  - an open body;\n  - an inward cavity shell (sliced alone it would read as material, and the union would fill the cavity).\n- A mesh that sliced before never reaches the fallback, so every existing CL/G-code golden is untouched by construction.\n- The refusal is reworded to name the model and the fix: \"the model's surfaces meet 3 or more ways at z = ... (non-manifold contact: solids welded along a shared edge or face, or a shell touching itself) - repair the mesh, or keep each solid a separate closed shell\".\n- New `GenError::Model`: the app and motion `from_slice` maps send `Open` and `NonManifold` there, so the message reads \"the source model cannot be sliced: ...\" instead of \"invalid machining parameters: ...\".\n- `material_above_of` and `material_overhead_of` move with the fallback into `slice_bodies.rs` and are re-exported from `slice`. `slice.rs` goes from 466 to 423 lines.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1407-shared-face-slice.md`. Sources: Requicha 1980 (sections of a regularized union), Botsch et al. 2010 (closed oriented 2-manifold test), Zhang & Chen 2001 (signed volume), Teschner et al. 2003 (spatial-hash weld).\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs`\n  - `the_sample_laid_flat_generates_3d_finish_and_pocket_with_no_gouge`: the issue's MCP job, laid flat. Both R1 and S1 now report `status: ok`, the program gate (stock sim) is `ok` with no gouge, and every finish-envelope gouge reading is under 0.01 mm.\n  - `the_laid_flat_band_sections_as_the_union_of_the_solids`: every plane in z 1.60 .. 3.15 sections, wider than the lower solid alone, and the islands law reads it.\n  - `the_sample_as_imported_still_sections_on_the_plain_read`: 240 planes over the as-imported span all slice.\n  - `welded_non_manifold_solids_are_refused_as_a_model_fault`: two blocks welded along one edge, through 3D Pocket. Refused with \"the source model cannot be sliced ... non-manifold\", and never \"invalid machining parameters\".\n  - `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_both_operations`: `#[ignore]`, heavy lane. The as-imported job spans 118 mm of Z and takes over 15 min in debug.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/slice_bodies.rs`: stacked solids, solids touching along a face, welded shared edge still refused (with the new wording), inward cavity shell refused (not filled), open solid refused, nanometre seam drift still welds.\n- `crates/motion/tests/islands_model_fault.rs`: `machining3d::material_above` returns `GenError::Model` for the welded soup and the union for stacked solids.\n\nMutation checks (STANDING RULE). Each line was deleted or changed, the pinning tests went RED, then it was restored and they went GREEN:\n\n| Mutation | RED tests |\n|---|---|\n| M1: drop the fallback call in `slice()` | stacked, touching, drift (geometry); laid-flat band and laid-flat generate (app) |\n| M2: drop the closed/consistent edge guard | `a_soup_with_an_open_solid_is_refused` |\n| M3: drop the outward (positive volume) guard | `a_soup_with_an_inward_cavity_shell_is_refused_not_filled` |\n| M4: weld tolerance 1e-4 -> 1e-12 mm | `nanometre_seam_drift_still_reads_closed_solids`, laid-flat band, laid-flat generate |\n| M5: restore the old refusal wording | `solids_welded_along_a_shared_edge_are_still_refused` |\n| M6: drop the app `from_slice` Model map | `welded_non_manifold_solids_are_refused_as_a_model_fault` |\n| M7: drop the motion `from_slice` Model map | `a_welded_non_manifold_soup_is_refused_as_a_model_fault` |\n\nAll restored: geometry 6/6, app 4/4 (+1 ignored), motion 2/2.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, which falls back to batch for a geometry change) on head `6726c1b8`: green except the ui step, where `trace_composite` and `trace_parity` died with SIGSEGV under 6 test threads. These are the software-GPU (`headless_gpu`) suites, and this diff touches no ui or trace code. Re-run on the same binaries with `--test-threads=1`, they pass: 5/5 and 4/4. Steps: geometry, cl, tools, post, sim, motion and app suites ok (app 1194 s); clippy ok; wall 31.7 min. Clippy `-D warnings` on geometry, motion, app and ui: clean.\n\nGoldens: none changed. The fallback only runs where the old code refused.\n\n## Not exercised / left open\n\n- On the laid-flat sample, the finish envelope's **rest** half still holds S1's post: \"finish envelope near move 2728: 0.0081 mm gouge, 4.5756 mm rest\". The gouge reading is under the gate; the rest is the steep walls a parallel finish leaves. The same finding appears on the body pairs that never needed the union (bodies 0+2: 3.17 mm rest; bodies 1+2: 3.17 mm), so it is how 3D Finish behaves on this geometry, not something this fix introduced. The post is held, never silently passed.\n- The heavy as-imported generation test was not run here.\n- `GenError` gains a variant. One exhaustive match in a test (`motion/tests/ruling.rs`) was updated.\n\nChangelog: 3D Finish and 3D Pocket machine a model made of stacked or touching closed solids (such as the sample STEP laid flat) as their union; genuine non-manifold meshes are refused as a model fault, not as invalid machining parameters (#1407)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation). Branched from upstream/main 3f6ecb4a; fork synced at v0.18.0, PROCESS_VERSION 54.\n\nFixes #1407\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
